TNT Installation Instructions
-----------------------------

TNT is free software. These instructions explain how to configure,
build, and install TNT from the source code.

Prerequisites
-------------

To compile TNT, you will need:

  * C, C++, and Fortran compilers
  * Tcl/Tk runtime and development packages
  * Optional documentation tools: pdflatex and latex2html

On Ubuntu/Debian systems, the following packages cover the build
requirements and runtime dependencies:

  sudo apt-get update
  sudo apt-get install -y \
    autoconf automake libtool gfortran \
    tcl tcl-dev tk tk-dev tcllib bwidget tcl-itcl4 iwidgets4 \
    texlive-latex-base latex2html

Compiling and Installing TNT
----------------------------

From the top-level source directory, bootstrap Autotools (including
subdirectories), configure, and build:

  ./bootstrap
  for dir in bem calcCAP calcRL csdl gui sppdgTcllib units; do \
    (cd "$dir" && ./bootstrap); \
  done
  for dir in sppdgTcllib/addressDialog sppdgTcllib/console \
             sppdgTcllib/getFilePreview sppdgTcllib/sgraph; do \
    (cd "$dir" && ./bootstrap); \
  done
  ./configure --prefix=/location/to/install/tnt
  make

Optional checks can be run with:

  make check

Required test (impedance example)
---------------------------------

To run the BEM test driver and validate impedance output against the
stored results, execute:

  wish bem/tests/test_bem.tcl

The test log is written to bem/tests/test_bem.log. The example impedance
output referenced in documentation is stored in bem/tests/test1.result.

Install with:

  make install

The configure script will analyze your system and generate makefiles
with the proper flags and macros. You should use the --prefix option to
control the installation location. Configure's --help option lists other
options and defaults.

To choose a different compiler, you can set environment variables or
set flags on the configure command line, for example:

  ./configure CC=c89 CXX=CC F77=f90

Running TNT
-----------

Running TNT requires a functioning installation of Tcl with Tk,
BWidget, Incr Tcl, and IWidgets extensions. These are available in
source code form from http://tcl.sourceforge.net/,
http://tcllib.sourceforge.net/, and http://incrtcl.sourceforge.net/.
You may also get a pre-compiled package called ActiveTcl from
http://activestate.com/tcl/.

To run TNT, make sure that the TNT package /bin directory and the wish
interpreter are both in your PATH. Run tnt from the command line or
from a shortcut. See the user guide for details on TNT operation.

Installing on Microsoft Windows
-------------------------------

TNT has been compiled and installed on Microsoft Windows computers
using the Cygwin development package from
http://sources.redhat.com/cygwin/. The same configure/make/make
install process described for Unix systems should work from the Cygwin
command window.

If you get the Windows binary installation of TNT, then compiling and
installing from the command line will not be necessary. Just follow
the usual installation procedures for Windows applications.
